{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/896628-more-than-one-totem-spirit-for-a-pack","id":896628,"title":"more than one totem spirit for a pack","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-23T01:23:03-07:00","id":896628,"title":"more than one totem spirit for a pack","content":"One of the HR's i started using way back when, was allowing a group who starts with a totem, to eventually quest to acquire a 2nd (or even third if they had good renown), but all totems need to be linked.. Such as having wolverine as base (gives rage and stamina) and taking boar (who also gives rage and stamina)..<br /> <br /> Have any of you tried that? How well did it work out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T05:54:00-07:00","id":896718,"title":"","content":"Uh. Why would a spirit ever agree to share the power, adoration and mystic oomph with another entity? Any pack seeking to do this would be doing a horrible disservice to their Totem, possibly giving it reason to abandon them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:46:04-07:00","id":896758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/896628-more-than-one-totem-spirit-for-a-pack?p=896718#post896718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. Why would a spirit ever agree to share the power, adoration and mystic oomph with another entity? Any pack seeking to do this would be doing a horrible disservice to their Totem, possibly giving it reason to abandon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the two totem spirits get along?<br /> Maybe the Pack - and specifically, select members of the Pack - went on really arduous and impressive quests.<br /> Maybe they don't mind sharing, if I dare to suggest such a possibility? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:07:17-07:00","id":896770,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure totems don't like to share","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:07:50-07:00","id":896771,"title":"","content":"The only canon bit where stuff like that would happen involves the Phoenix. And if Phoenix takes you, your old totem is not staying. On the offchance you don't die doing the Pheoenixes bidding, and/or end your stint with the Silver Pack it will absolve you and you might petition to your old totem to return you into the fold.<br /> <br /> Totems only serve the pack because the pack serves them. There is no benefit in sharing this service with anyone else, as the pack is the only way for a spirit to gain power and prestige and become &quot;someone&quot; in the hieararchy of its host.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 05-23-2016, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:34:37-07:00","id":896800,"title":"","content":"This house rule has two parts.<br /> Mechanically, is the question if PCs can spend unlimited XP on totem, or if they are limited to five per character, because backgrounds are limited to five. If you have the limit, adding additional totems is kind of limited, if you have only one pool to buy the totems. Still, doesn't make much sense to have more than one, as a game benefit. Boosting the totem you already have to have the benefits for more PCs at the same time and so on, usually is a better choice.<br /> <br /> In-Game wise, totems are not spirits that only follow the pack. It is a semi-godlike entity, who if a pack pledges allegiance will get rewards, and an relatively weak avatar of said Incarnae being. So, such a pledge for allegiance is probably exclusive, at least among other totems. Jamie Lannister states at one point in the books, that each knight has to many oaths to swear, that they are bound to break some. And surely, a totem accepts that a pack has obligations to sept, septleader, family and such. But that they serve two totems, even those who are kin of similar seems far fetched...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:31:22-07:00","id":896843,"title":"","content":"We'll be running into that problem shortly when our 3rd edition Ahadi group will become a W20 Kganmadi and all the Bastet players would have to ditch their beloved Jamak. I'm thinking strongly about throwing canon out of the window here to keep the players happy. :-/ Doesn't feel so right, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T11:17:59-07:00","id":896985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taci</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/896628-more-than-one-totem-spirit-for-a-pack?p=896843#post896843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll be running into that problem shortly when our 3rd edition Ahadi group will become a W20 Kganmadi and all the Bastet players would have to ditch their beloved Jamak. I'm thinking strongly about throwing canon out of the window here to keep the players happy. :-/ Doesn't feel so right, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bIs this a personal Jamak, or a 'Pride' Jamak? The former struck me as a lot less formal than the latter. (Based on respect, trust, and friendship rather than mutual service.)<br /> <br /> I want to say one of the Tribebooks had a similar background of 'Spirit Companion' or 'Spirit Ally' that was separate from the pack Totem that would be similar.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T11:23:21-07:00","id":896995,"title":"","content":"The most likely result of a Pack having two totems in my mind is that the two Totems will constantly be fighting over which of them gets your chiminage and provides you benefits. So you may be counting on Wolverine's Rage and get Boar's instead.<br /> <br /> And you'd have to follow both bans at all times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T12:08:05-07:00","id":897048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/896628-more-than-one-totem-spirit-for-a-pack?p=896758#post896758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/896628-more-than-one-totem-spirit-for-a-pack?p=896718#post896718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. Why would a spirit ever agree to share the power, adoration and mystic oomph with another entity? Any pack seeking to do this would be doing a horrible disservice to their Totem, possibly giving it reason to abandon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the two totem spirits get along?<br /> Maybe the Pack - and specifically, select members of the Pack - went on really arduous and impressive quests.<br /> Maybe they don't mind sharing, if I dare to suggest such a possibility? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Take Twister, a totem spirit of destruction. Now add to that say a spirit of chaos. Both of those i can easily see working together.<br /> OR as the example in my OP suggested, Boar and Wolverine (both totems of stamina and rage)..<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/896628-more-than-one-totem-spirit-for-a-pack?p=896995#post896995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most likely result of a Pack having two totems in my mind is that the two Totems will constantly be fighting over which of them gets your chiminage and provides you benefits. So you may be counting on Wolverine's Rage and get Boar's instead.<br /> <br /> And you'd have to follow both bans at all times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, they will have to follow both bans, and MAY get into conflicts on who's Chiminage gets precedent over the others.. Its not something that always came up, but three times i have seen a group try to get a 2nd totem. And once i knew a ST who let a player who had a Personal totem (via players book double cost), also benefit from a pack one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:09:03-07:00","id":897168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/896628-more-than-one-totem-spirit-for-a-pack?p=897048#post897048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And once i knew a ST who let a player who had a Personal totem (via players book double cost), also benefit from a pack one...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had a ST that ran the game like this. And while it did go against canon, within that game it worked out just fine. There was a lot of pressure to make sure the characters (there were 2 or 3) kept up on both bans and offering chiminages, but it worked and the game was a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:05:53-07:00","id":897357,"title":"","content":"That makes me wonder. who else HAS used the rule from the players guide to allow a Pc to get personal totems?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:05:07-07:00","id":897922,"title":"","content":"Personal totems by themselves aren't a terribly big deal. The problem is when you have a pack member (who has a pack totem) who wants a personal totem as well, which isn't allowed (or shouldn't be) per canon setting rules since, as stated above, Totems don't share.<br /> So I have been in a game where 1 PC specifically wasn't part of the pack because he wanted a personal totem. I don't think it was worth it personally. Especially in a pure werewolf game, losing pack benefits (and role playing) generally isn't worth being an outsider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 05-24-2016, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T04:40:25-07:00","id":898806,"title":"","content":"I think personal Totems can be done, since the Garou already have to share their respect and chiminage between their Pack Totem and Sept Totem.<br /> If you look at it this way, a Personal Totem can never be as strong as a Pack Totem which can never be as strong as a Sept Totem simply because you cannot put down more than 5 dots into a Totem yourself. If you have a pack of 4 Garou each putting the max amount into the Totem, that's a pretty powerful Totem. 4 times more powerful than the Personal Totem can be. By the same logic, each garou who give chiminage and pay respect to the Sept Totem makes that Totem more powerful. I don't think that spirits require you to only pay respect and chiminage to them, they should be ok with you having another spirit who you are especially close to, otherwise the whole Pack and Sept Totem thing should be able to work.<br /> <br /> Edit: i keep looking for a better phrase than &quot;pay chiminage to&quot; or &quot;pay respect to&quot;. Fealty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T02:00:04-07:00","id":903343,"title":"","content":"I would... not allow a pack to have 2 pack totems. But calling on Pack and Tribal totem is clearly something different. And personal totems are still a thing in a pack (or rather Kganmadi or Mountain Sentai - stuff like the Bastet Jamak. However, some personal totems might e more powerful than the pack totem - a Bastet with the Jamak &quot;Mistress of Catkind&quot; (*****) will still have a more powerful ally than the pack that follows the humble &quot;Butterfly&quot; (*). Hell, from some power aspect, some of the personal totems (King-of-Beasts, King of Cats and Mistress of Catkind) are Incarna, or at least aspects of them. Well, King-of-Beasts needs you to have one packmate to pay his 6-dots if I read him correctly, but then again he is Lion, he is the Tribal Totem of the (pride-forming) Simba and can be also the one of a pack.<br /> <br /> There are even some Fera, that are obligated to have a Totem: Ananasi for example [n]must[/b] be bonded to Ananasa in some type and all Nuwisha have one of Coyote's faces bond to them.<br /> And on the other hand, Nagah are banned from gaining any Totem but gain the pack tactics bonus nonetheless.<br /> <br /> And then again, there are those temporary packs - or rather the short-lived variants, Questing Kganmadi and the Wave Sentai - Pack Totem Not Included (but keep your personal one at will!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","user":"Hira Akigi","date":". 11-05-2016, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}